Serious suggestions:
	I second the idea of monsters that are too powerful to kill.
It is definitely one of the larger flaws in the game. "Puny Mortal."
The dragons, once you reach them, are entirely too easy.  At the very
least, make the 'kill' conditions more specific.  Make the Demon Lords
only defeatable by ultra-high level Lawful Clerics, for example.
Perhaps only certain beasts could be killed with certain weapons, such
as Trolls by Trollsbane (or a scroll/wand of light), or Dragons by
Dragonsbane. Add a true Balrog, or perhaps summon a Nazgul if you put
on the wrong Ring. Throw in a couple of Norse Gods. The possiblities
are endless.

Humorous suggestions:
	In previous versions (perhaps site-customized), there have
been unique characters that added to the charm of the game, such as
the 3 stooges, a white rabbit (I'm late!), the 7 dwarves, and Gandalf.
What happened to them? There have been recent suggestions to add
Cerebus (do you mean the Aardvark or the dog?), Inigo Montoya, Elric,
and the Killer Rabbit from Monty Python.
	Perhaps this could be combined with obtaining some of the
weapons that are unbelievably powerful; just _try_ to get Mjollnir
away from Thor, Stormbringer away from Elric, or Excalibur from King
Arthur!
	How about potential magic objects? The White Rabbit's watch
(time stop!), a Holy Hand Grenade, heck, a Holy Grail (perfect for
making holy water)!

	Right, enough bandwitdth wasted. Go to it. Tear it all to shreds.


